IMPORT prelude

-- Kidnapping Act 1961 (Singapore) -- the whole Act: kidnapping for ransom (s 3), receiving ransom (s 4), negotiating for or paying
-- ransom (s 5), freezing bank accounts (s 6), the duty to inform the police (s 9), and the evidence rules (ss 12 to 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/KA1961.txt. The deposit's
-- arrangement of sections runs one ahead of the body from s 7; the encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 14 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. Short enough to take whole; the Public
-- Prosecutor's investigative powers (ss 7, 8, 10) are summarised, not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Kidnapping Act 1961`

§§ `3 to 5 -- the offences`

-- s 3: abducting, wrongfully restraining or wrongfully confining a person "with intent to hold any person for ransom" -- DEATH or
-- imprisonment for life, and caning if not sentenced to death.
-- s 4: knowingly receiving, possessing or disposing of ransom -- up to 10 years and caning.
-- s 5(1): knowingly negotiating to OBTAIN ransom -- up to 10 years and caning. (2): knowingly negotiating to PAY, paying, or
-- PROVIDING FUNDS for a ransom -- up to 7 years and a fine.
--
-- s 5(2) makes it an offence for the victim's family to pay the ransom.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `kidnapping for ransom`
    `receiving the ransom knowingly`
    `negotiating to obtain the ransom`
    `paying the ransom`
    `lending money to the family to pay the ransom`
    `reporting the kidnapping to the police`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `reporting the kidnapping to the police` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A STRING
`the maximum sentence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `kidnapping for ransom` THEN "death or life imprisonment"
    WHEN `receiving the ransom knowingly` THEN "10 years and caning"
    WHEN `negotiating to obtain the ransom` THEN "10 years and caning"
    WHEN `paying the ransom` THEN "7 years and a fine"
    WHEN `lending money to the family to pay the ransom` THEN "7 years and a fine"
    OTHERWISE "none"

§§ `6 -- freezing bank accounts`

-- s 6(1): where the Public Prosecutor is satisfied that ransom is likely to be paid out of a bank account, he may order the bank not
-- to pay out of it "for a specified period not exceeding ONE MONTH". (2): bank officers who comply are relieved of liability. (3): a
-- bank manager who fails to comply -- $3,000 or 3 years.
GIVEN `days ordered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the freezing order is within the limit` IF
    `days ordered` AT MOST 31

§§ `9 -- the duty to inform the police`

-- s 9(1): "any person who is aware of the commission of or the intention of any other person to commit any offence under this Act
-- shall, in the absence of reasonable excuse, the BURDEN of proving which shall lie upon the person so aware, forthwith give
-- information to a police officer". (2): $1,000 or 12 months.
--
-- A relative who knows of the kidnapping and keeps quiet commits an offence unless they prove a reasonable excuse.
GIVEN `was aware` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed the police forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to inform is an offence` IF
    `was aware` AND (NOT `informed the police forthwith`) AND (NOT `proved a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `12 to 14 -- evidence`

-- s 12: no witness is "presumed to be unworthy of credit by reason only that he has paid or negotiated to pay any ransom".
-- s 13(1): unexplained wealth disproportionate to known income, or an unexplained accretion at about the time, may be taken as
-- CORROBORATING testimony that the accused received a ransom. (2): including property held by others on the accused's behalf.
-- s 14: an informer's identity is protected, (3) unless the informer knowingly lied or justice cannot otherwise be done.
GIVEN `has unexplained wealth disproportionate to income` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is witness testimony of receipt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wealth may corroborate the testimony` IF
    `has unexplained wealth disproportionate to income` AND `there is witness testimony of receipt`

GIVEN `the informer knowingly lied` IS A BOOLEAN, `justice requires disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may require the informer to be disclosed` IF
    `the informer knowingly lied` OR `justice requires disclosure`
